;; review4 bug-08 (pre-existing twin, newly common now that 5+ arity fns
;; lower): complement's twin (rt/wasm/core.lg:543) fills Fn slots 0..4 only
;; and FnInfo k = -1, so a complemented fn called or applied with 5+ args
;; raises an arity error whose text prints k as unsigned ("expected
;; 4294967295 args"). Native's complemented-fn takes any arg count.
;; Same shape to check: rt/wasm/lang.lg:108 (FnInfo 0 -1, null slots).
;; native lg 4e769212 prints:
;; true
;; false
(println ((complement (fn [& xs] false)) 1 2 3 4 5))
(println (apply (complement (fn [a b c d e] true)) [1 2 3 4 5]))
